# See https://docs.github.com/en/get-started/getting-started-with-git/ignoring-files for more about ignoring files.

# Environment variables — never commit real credentials
# Every .env variant is secret-bearing. Backups like `.env.bak-19k` were
# NOT matched by the old three-pattern list and would have been committed.
.env*
!.env.example

# compiled output
dist
tmp
out-tsc
*.tsbuildinfo
.expo
.expo-shared

# dependencies
node_modules

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.venv/
venv/

# Test coverage
.coverage
.coverage.*
coverage.xml
htmlcov/

# IDEs and editors
/.idea
.project
.classpath
.c9/
*.launch
.settings/
*.sublime-workspace

# IDE - VSCode
.vscode/*
!.vscode/settings.json
!.vscode/tasks.json
!.vscode/launch.json
!.vscode/extensions.json

# misc
/.sass-cache
/connect.lock
/coverage
/libpeerconnection.log
npm-debug.log
yarn-error.log
testem.log
/typings

# System Files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

.cursor/rules/nx-rules.mdc
.github/instructions/nx.instructions.md

# Local Neo4j instance (data + binaries)
.neo4j/
neo4j_data/
neo4j_logs/

# Runtime state — data, not source. Cloned repos land in $WORKSPACE_DIR,
# which defaults to /tmp outside the tree and is a Docker named volume
# in compose (docker-compose.yml), never a path under the repo.
var/
*.pid

# Working artifacts of building this, not part of what is published.
# The roadmap CSVs are a closed task list (89/89) and a capability matrix
# kept alongside it; `.agents/memory` is an agent's notes between sessions.
# Nothing in the tree may read them — `test_source_hygiene.py` carries its
# own frozen copy of the ids for exactly that reason.
docs/design/*-roadmap.csv
.agents/

# Pasted conversation fragments. They arrive with a `Pasted-...` name, carry
# whatever was on the clipboard — another project's tracker ids, findings
# about a running system — and are nobody's source.
attached_assets/

# Scaffolding assistants and their plugins drop into a checkout. None of it
# is here today; these are listed so it cannot arrive in a commit later,
# when it would read as part of the project. `AGENTS.md` and `CLAUDE.md` are
# deliberately NOT ignored — they are the written rules, not tool state.
.claude/
.superpowers/
.cursor/
.windsurf/
.aider*
.github/copilot-instructions.md
**/skills/*/SKILL.md
.mcp.json
